excerpt: "Statement-Conclusion ke saare niyam, Venn diagram soch aur solved examples ke saath poori taiyari.",
body: `
<h2>Parichay</h2><p>Statement-Conclusion reasoning ka sabse zyada poochha jaane wala topic hai. Isme kuch kathan diye jaate hain aur unke neeche kuch nishkarsh diye jaate hain. Aapko yeh tay karna hota hai ki kaun sa nishkarsh kathanon se tarkik roop se nikalta hai. Sabse bada niyam yeh hai ki kathanon ko satya maan kar chalna hai, chahe vaastavik duniya me woh galat lagte hon. Udaaharan ke liye, agar kathan kahe ki saare billi kutte hain, to aapko use satya maan na hai aur usi aadhaar par nishkarsh jaanchna hai.</p><h2>Zaroori Niyam</h2><ul><li>Keval wahi nishkarsh sahi hai jo kathanon se pakke taur par nikalta ho. Sambhavna par aadhaarit nishkarsh galat hota hai.</li><li>All ka ulta Some hota hai. Matlab, agar saare A, B hain to kuch B, A zaroor hain.</li><li>Some ka ulta bhi Some hota hai. Agar kuch A, B hain to kuch B, A bhi hain.</li><li>No ka ulta No hota hai. Agar koi A, B nahi hai to koi B, A bhi nahi hai.</li><li>All ke saath All judta hai. Saare A, B hain aur saare B, C hain to saare A, C hain.</li><li>Some ke saath All judta hai, lekin All ke saath Some nahi judta. Kuch A, B hain aur saare B, C hain to kuch A, C hain. Lekin saare A, B hain aur kuch B, C hain to kuch A, C ke baare me kuch pakka nahi keh sakte.</li><li>No ke saath All ka natija kabhi All nahi hota, keval Some-not nikal sakta hai.</li><li>Doosre gyaan ya samanya jaankari se nishkarsh mat nikalo, keval diye gaye kathanon se nikalo.</li></ul><h2>Solved Example 1</h2><p>Kathan: Saare pen, kitaab hain. Saare kitaab, kursi hain. Nishkarsh 1: Kuch pen, kursi hain. Nishkarsh 2: Saare kursi, pen hain. Pehla nishkarsh sahi hai kyunki pen, kitaab ke andar hain aur kitaab, kursi ke andar hain, isliye pen kursi ke andar hain. Doosra nishkarsh galat hai kyunki kursi ka daira bada hai, usme pen ke alawa bhi bahut kuch ho sakta hai. Isliye keval nishkarsh 1 sahi hai.</p><h2>Solved Example 2</h2><p>Kathan: Kuch billi, kutte hain. Saare kutte, jaanwar hain. Nishkarsh 1: Kuch billi, jaanwar hain. Nishkarsh 2: Kuch jaanwar, billi hain. Dono sahi hain. Pehla isliye kyunki jo billi kutte hain, woh jaanwar bhi hain. Doosra pehle ka ulta hai, aur Some ka ulta hamesha sahi hota hai.</p><h2>Solved Example 3</h2><p>Kathan: Koi phool, phal nahi hai. Saare phal, ped hain. Nishkarsh 1: Koi phool, ped nahi hai. Nishkarsh 2: Kuch ped, phool nahi hain. Pehla galat hai kyunki ped ka daira phal se bada hai, koi phool aisa ped ho sakta hai jo phal na ho. Doosra sahi hai kyunki jo phal hain woh ped hain aur phool nahi hain, isliye kuch ped pakke taur par phool nahi hain. Isliye keval nishkarsh 2 sahi hai.</p><h2>Tricks aur Aam Galtiyan</h2><p>Venn diagram banane ki aadat dalo. Bade circle ke andar chhota circle All ko dikhata hai, katte hue circle Some ko dikhate hain, aur alag circle No ko dikhate hain. Aam galti yeh hoti hai ki chhatra ulta nishkarsh ko sahi maan lete hain, jaise saare A, B hain to saare B, A hain keh dena. Yeh galat hai. Doosri galti yeh hai ki sambhavna ko nishkarsh maan lena. Agar kuch ho sakta hai, to woh nishkarsh nahi hai. Nishkarsh wahi hai jo har haal me satya ho. Teesri galti vaastavik duniya ka gyaan lagana hai. Kathan ko hi antim satya mano.</p><blockquote>Yaad rakho: Nishkarsh pakka hona chahiye, sambhav nahi. Pakka nahi to galat.</blockquote>
`
